    "title": "אַף־עַל־גַב דַּאֲנָא | Af Al Gav Da-ana — an original Aramaic “Meturgeman piyyuṭ” for Simḥat Torah by Isaac Gantwerk Mayer",
    "author": "Isaac Gantwerk Mayer",
    "coauthors": [
        {
            "name": "Isaac Gantwerk Mayer",
            "bio": "From a family of musicians, Isaac Gantwerk Mayer believes that creative art is one of the most powerful ways to get in touch with the divine. He composes music and poetry in Hebrew and English. (He also <a href=\"/index.php?user_ID=342\">translates</a> and <a href=\"/index.php?user_ID=820\">transcribes</a> Hebrew and Aramaic texts, adding <em>niqqud</em> and <em>t'amim</em> as needed.) Isaac runs a Jewish music transcription service, which will transcribe and set any Jewish music in any language, recorded or written. Contact his service on <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/pg/isaacgmayerjewishtranscription/\">Facebook</a> or via <a href=\"https://igmjewishcreativeworks.com/contact\">his music blog</a>.",
            "website": "https://igmjewishcreativeworks.com",
            "avatar": "https://opensiddur.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/12/isaac-gantwerk-mayer-2021-e1674561264977-96x96.jpg",
            "profile_link": "https://opensiddur.org/profile/isaac-gantwerk-mayer"
        }
    ],
    "date": "2026-09-14",
    "last_updated": "2026-09-25",
    "excerpt": "An original Aramaic-language “meturgeman piyyut” for Simḥat Torah. I’m working on creating a seder meturgeman liturgy, akin to those for day 7 of Pesaḥ and for Shavuot, to be recited on Simḥat Torah. Mostly incorporating older Aramaic poems, I’ve also decided to write some originals myself. This piyyut, written in the structure of the famous Aqdamut Milin reshut still recited on Shavuot, is meant to be inserted before the translation of the first verse of the first aliyah on Simḥat Torah. It discusses the halakhic status and history of Shmini Atzeret, as well as the final blessing and death of Moses.",
    "content": "<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"font-size: 1.2em;\">\nAn original Aramaic-language “meturgeman piyyuṭ” for Simḥat Torah. I’m working on creating a seder meturgeman liturgy, akin to those for day 7 of Pesaḥ and for Shavuot, to be recited on Simḥat Torah. Mostly incorporating older Aramaic poems, I’ve also decided to write some originals myself. This piyyuṭ, written in the structure of the famous Aqdamut Milin reshut still recited on Shavuot, is meant to be inserted before the translation of the first verse of the first aliyah on Simḥat Torah. It discusses the halakhic status and history of Shmini Atseret, as well as the final blessing and death of Moses.\n</div>\n<hr />\n<table style=\"margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" class=\"draggable toggleable-table\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th id=\"x\" style=\"text-align: right;\">Source (Hebrew)</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">Translation (English)</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span class=\"acrostic\">אַ</span>ף־עַל־גַב דַּאֲנָא זְעֵיר בְּחׇכְמְתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">אֲ</span>קוּם כְּעַן לְשַׁכְלָלָא וּלְאַתְחוֹלֵי תַּרְגּוּמָא דְּאוֹרָיְתָּא\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nAlthough I am small in wisdom, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nI will stand here to finish and begin the translation of the Torah. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span class=\"acrostic\">בְּ</span>יוֹמָא תְּמִינָאָה דְּאִתְקְרֵי עֲצַרְתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">בְּ</span>עֶסְרִין וּתְרֵין לְיַרְחָא דְתִשְׁרֵי עֶסְרִין וּתְלָת בְּגָלוּתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">גּ</span>וּנְדֵי עַם חַבִּיב נְפַקוּ מִן־מְטַלְּתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">גְּ</span>נוּנָא דַּחֲתָנָא דְחָדֵי עִם־כַּלְּתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">דִּ</span>בְחַגָּא רַבָּא מִן־כָּל מְאַרְעֵי בְּחֶדְוָתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">דְּ</span>אִתְקְרֵי עַל־שׁוּם דִמְטַלַּיָּא דְּתוֹתַבְתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">הָ</span>אִידָּנָא זִימְנָא לְגַרְמֵיהּ לְבְקִיאֵי דַּתָּא\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nOn the eighth day that is called &#8220;Gathering,&#8221; <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nThe twenty-second of the month of Tishri, twenty-third in diaspora, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nThe troops of the beloved people went out from the sukkah, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nThe wedding-chamber of the groom who rejoices with the bride, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nWithin the festival greatest of all occasions in joy, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nAs referred to by the name of the sukkot of temporary dwelling. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nNow is its own time, according to the experts of law. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span class=\"acrostic\">ה</span>וּא מִיפָּרַשׁ מִן־בַּתְרֵיהּ לְעִנְיָנִין שִׁתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">וְ</span>סִימָנָךְ פָּזֵ״‎ר קֶֽשֶׁ״‎ב כִּגְּמִירִינַן בְּבָרַיְתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">וְ</span>הָא בְּגוֹ פִירְקָא רְבִיעָאָה דְּמַסֶּכְתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">זְ</span>רִיזֵי כְּהוּנְּתָא רְהַטוּ לִפְיָסָא חַדְתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">זִ</span>ימְנָא מְבָרְכִינַן וְשֶׁהֶחֱיָנוּ הִיא בִּרְכְתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">חַ</span>גָּא לְגַרְמֵיהּ הוּא וְלָא צְרִיכָא לְמֵיתַב בִּמְטַלְּתָּא\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nIt it distinguished after it for six matters.<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_1');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_1');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_1\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[1]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_1\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Shmini Atseret is distinguished from Sukkot in six ways.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_1').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_1', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nAnd your mnemonic is PaZe&#8221;R KeShe&#8221;V, as we were taught in a baraita, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nwhich is in the fourth chapter of the tractate:<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_2');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_2');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_2\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[2]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_2\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Sukkah 48a&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_2').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_2', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nThe swiftest of the priesthood ran to a new lottery. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nWe bless the time and Sheheḥeyanu is the blessing. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nIt is its own festival, and it is unnecessary to reside in sukkot. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span class=\"acrostic\">חַ</span>ד תּוֹרָא לְמִיקָרְבֵּיהּ קוּרְבַּן עֲלָתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">טְ</span>עִינֵי מָאנֵי קוּדְשָׁא חַלְפוּן שִׁירָתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">ט</span>וּפְסָא דְּיַעֲלֵה וְיָבוֹא אִיחַלַּף בִּצְלוֹתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">י</span>וֹמָא דֵּין נֵימָא אָתֵיב רוּחָא וּמָחֵית מִיטְרָא בִּגְבוּרְתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">יִ</span>תּוֹסַף בְּמוּסָפָא דְאַָתֵי בְּאַרְעָא וּכְבַר אִתּוֹסַף בְּאוּמָּתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">כִּ</span>י יֵיתוּן חַמְשִׁין יוֹמִין בֵּין פִּסְחָא לַעֲצַרְתָּא בְּתַרְתָּא\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nOne bull is to be offered as a wholly burnt offering. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nThe bearers of the sacred vessels changed the song. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nThe form of &#8220;Ya&#8217;aleh v-Yavo&#8221; is changed in prayer. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nThis day we say &#8220;Returning wind and bringing down rain&#8221; in the blessing of Strength, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nAdded in an additional service to come in the land, and already added in the nations. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nBut fifty days come between Pesaḥ and the prior gathering!<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_3');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_3');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_3\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[3]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_3\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Shavuot, also called “Gathering” in rabbinic texts.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_3').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_3', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span class=\"acrostic\">כִּ</span>דְלָא מְשַׁהֵינַן עַד יַרְחָא תְּשִׁיעַיְתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">לְ</span>פוּם דְּמִטְרָא בְּסִתְוָא הוּא עִיקָּר טַרְחוּתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">לָ</span>כֵן אֲמַר קוּדְשָׁא בְּרִיךְ הוּא שְׁהוּ גַבַּי הַשְׁתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">מַ</span>תְלָא אַמְתֵּיל לְמָאי דָמֵי מִלְּתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">מַ</span>לְכָּא דְּבִיסְרָא וְאַדְמָא דִּמְזַמָּן סְעוֹדְתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">נְ</span>זַמֵּן לְאוּשְׁפִּיזִין מִן־שַׁבְעִין מְדִינָתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">נֵ</span>יכוֹל וְנִשְׁתֵּי וּנְחַדֵּי כׇּל־שְׁבַעְתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">סִ</span>יוּמָא דְּיוֹמִין אֲמַר לְחַד בַּר הֵימָנוּתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">סַ</span>גִּיאִין שְׁבַקוּ אַנְתְּ שְׁהִי כַּאן בִּרְשׁוּתָּא\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nWhy do we not wait until the ninth month? <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nOn account of the winter rain, which is the ultimate trouble<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_4');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_4');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_4\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[4]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_4\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Shir haShirim Rabbah 2:11:1&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_4').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_4', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nThus <span class=\"divine-referent\">the Blessed Holy One</span> said, &#8220;Wait with Me here.&#8221; <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nAn allegory I will allege: what is this matter like? <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nA king of flesh and blood who was hosting a feast. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\n&#8220;Let us invite guests from seventy nations, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nLet us eat and drink and rejoice all week!&#8221; <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nAt the end of the days he said to one faithful one, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\n&#8220;The crowds have left. You, stay here in my domain!&#8221;<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_5');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_5');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_5\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[5]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_5\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Sukkah 55b&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_5').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_5', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span class=\"acrostic\">עָ</span>לָוָן שַׁבְעִין קָרִיבוּ לְשַׁבְעִין אוּמָּתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">עַ</span>ל־כֵּן בִּלְחוֹדֵהוֹן תּוֹר חַד דְּכַר חַד לַעֲלָתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">פַּ</span>לְטֵרִין חֲנֵיךְ שְׁלֹמֹה מַלְכָּא בְּחֲנֻכַּת בֵּיתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">פַּ</span>יֵּיס וְצַלֵּי בְּיוֹמָא דֵּין וּנְכֵס סַגִּי נִכְסָתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">צְ</span>לוֹתֵיהּ בְּדִיל עַמֵּיהּ עִמֵּיהּ מִנַחֲלָא דְמִצְרַיִם לְמַעֲלָנָא דַחֲמָתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">צָ</span>וַח וַאֲמַר וִיהֵי לִבְּכוֹן שְׁלִים וּלְמִטַּר פִּקּוּדוֹהִי בִּדְחַלְתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">קָ</span>רִיבוּ תַּרְתֵּין רִבּוֹא וּתְרֵין אַלְפִין תּוֹרֵי וַעֲנָא רִבּוֹא עַסְרֵי וְתַרְתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">קֳ</span>דָם קוּדְשָׁא בְּרִיךְ הוּא שְׁמִיעַ כׇּל־צְלוֹתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">רְ</span>שׁוּתָא לְמִכְפַל לְאַרְבֵּיסַר יוֹמֵי קַבֵּל קֹהֶֽלֶת בְּבִינְתָּא\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nSeventy offerings they offered for seventy nations, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nSo only one ox and one ram are for burnt-offerings. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nKing Solomon dedicated a palace in the dedication of the House. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nHe pleaded and prayed on this day and slaughtered many sacrifices. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nHis prayer was on behalf of his people with him from the wadi of Egypt to the ascent of Ḥamat,<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_6');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_6');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_6\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[6]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_6\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> I Kings 8:65&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_6').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_6', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nAnd he cried out and said &#8220;May you wholeheartedly keep <span class=\"divine-referent\">Their</span> commandments in awe!&#8221; <span class=\"citation\">(I Kings 8:61)</span> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nThey slaughtered 22,000 cattle and 120,000 sheep<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_7');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_7');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_7\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[7]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_7\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> I Kings 8:64&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_7').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_7', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nBefore <span class=\"divine-referent\">the Blessed Holy One</span>, <span class=\"divine-referent\">Hearer of all prayer</span>. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nPermission to double it to fourteen days Ḳohelet<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_8');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_8');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_8\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[8]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_8\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Solomon&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_8').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_8', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> acquired with understanding.<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_9');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_9');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_9\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[9]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_9\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> I Kings 8:65&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_9').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_9', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span class=\"acrostic\">רַ</span>בָּא דְּכָהֲנֵי וְסָפְרֵי נְטַר יוֹמָא דֵּין עִם־תִּרְשָׁתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">שְׁ</span>מָעוּ עַמָּא מֵימַר קַדִּישָׁא דִּכְתִיב בְּאוֹרָיְתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">שָׁ</span>קֵיהוֹן מְחוֹ וַהֲדָרוּ בְּתִיוּבְתָּא\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nThe greatest of priests and scribes<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_10');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_10');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_10\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[10]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_10\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Ezra&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_10').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_10', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> kept this day with the Tirshatha.<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_11');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_11');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_11\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[11]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_11\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Nehemiah&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_11').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_11', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nThe people heard the holy word written in the Torah.<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_12');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_12');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_12\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[12]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_12\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Nehemiah 8:18&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_12').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_12', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nThey struck their thighs<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_13');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_13');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_13\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[13]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_13\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> An expression of self-reproach. Find Jeremiah 31:19&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_13').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_13', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> and returned in repentance. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span class=\"acrostic\">תַּ</span>קִּינוּ רַבָּנַן לְמִקְרֵי כׇּל־אוֹרָיְתָא חֲדָא בְּשַׁתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">תְּ</span>שַׁכְלְלוּנַּהּ כְּעַן אֲמַרוּ וּמֵאַלְתַּר תַּתְחֲלוּן אוֹרָיְתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">י</span>וֹמִין דְּחִילִין כֻּלְּהוֹן תַּעַבְרוּן מֵרֵישָׁא דְּשַׁתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">צ</span>וֹמָא רַבָּא עַסְרָא יוֹמִין בַּתְרוֹהִי יוֹמֵי דְּתִיוּבְתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">חַ</span>גָּא דִמְטַלַּיָּא חַמְשָׁא יוֹמִין בַּתָר כַּפָּרָא דְּחַטָּאתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">קַ</span>דִּישִׁין מֵאַרְעִין אִלֵּין וּמְמַלְּלִינָן פִּתְגָּמֵי תּוּשְׁבַּחְתָּא\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nOur rabbis established to read all the Torah once a year. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\n&#8220;Finish it now,&#8221; they said, &#8220;and immediately start the Torah.&#8221; <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nDays of awe have all passed, from the new year;<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_14');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_14');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_14\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[14]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_14\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Rosh haShanah&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_14').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_14', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nThe great fast<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_15');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_15');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_15\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[15]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_15\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Yom Kippur&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_15').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_15', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> ten days after it, days of repentance, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nThe festival of sukkot five days after the atonement of sin. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nThese occasions are holy, and on them we say words of praise. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span class=\"acrostic\">הֵ</span>יכְדֵין אַף עַל־מֹשֶׁה רַבָּנָא קָם מַלְאֲכָא דְמוֹתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">רְ</span>שׁוּתֵיהּ הִיא עַל־כׇּל־אִינְשֵׁי מִיּוֹם אִיתְרִיכוּ מִגִּינְתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">אֲ</span>מַר מֹשֶׁה בְּבָעוּ אֵעִבַר וְאֶחֱזֵי יָת־אַרְעָא טַבְתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">לָ</span>א־קַבִּיל מִנֵּיהּ רִבּוֹן עָלְמִין וַאֲמַר סַק לְרֵישׁ רָמָתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">ה</span>וּא מִילֵּל בְּמֵישְׁרָא דְּמוֹאָב בָּתַר אַרְבְּעִין שַׁתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">כׇּ</span>ל־פַּתְשֶֽׁגֶן אוֹרָֽיְתָא הָדָא בְּיוֹם מַפְּקָנוּת נִשְׁמְתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">ה</span>וּא יוֹם בֵּית וַלְדָּא דִּדֵּיהּ לְפוּם חוּלָקָא דְּצִדְקוּתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">נְ</span>פַקָא לֵיהּ נִשְׁמְתֵיהּ בִּשְׁבִיעָאָה דְּיַרְחָא לְמַסְגֵּי בְּחֶדְוְתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">בְּ</span>יוֹמָא הוּא קַבֵּל רַבָּנָא חוּלָקֵיהּ בִּשְׁרִירוּתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">נְ</span>בוֹ מַתְקַן לְקִבְלֵיהּ אַיָּדֵי מַלְאָכַיָּא דְּמַשְׁרִיתָּא\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nHence even upon Moshe our teacher rose the angel of death, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nWhose domain is over all people since the day they were expelled from the garden. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nMoshe said, &#8220;Please, let me pass, that I may see the good land!&#8221; <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\n<span class=\"divine-referent\">The Master of Eternities</span> did not accept him, and said, &#8220;Go up to the mountaintop.&#8221; <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nHe spoke in the plain of Moab after forty years, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nAll this copy of the Torah<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_16');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_16');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_16\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[16]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_16\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Deuteronomy, which is largely the final speech of Moses. Find Deuteronomy 17:18.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_16').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_16', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> on the day his soul left. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nIt was his birthday, as is the portion of the righteous.<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_17');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_17');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_17\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[17]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_17\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Kiddushin 38a&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_17').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_17', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nHis soul left him on the seventh of the month of increasing in happiness.<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_18');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_18');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_18\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[18]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_18\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Adar&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_18').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_18', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nOn that day our master received his portion in truth <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nNebo was prepared to accept him by the hands of ministering angels.<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_19');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_19');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_19\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[19]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_19\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Targum Pseudo-Jonathan on Deuteronomy 34:6&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_19').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_19', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span class=\"acrostic\">אֲ</span>מַר נְבִיָּא דִּנְבִיִּין בְּיוֹם דְּיִקְבַּל מוֹתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">בִּ</span>רְכָן לְכׇל־שִׁבְטַיָּא לְכׇל־בַּר שְׁלִים יְהַב חֲדָא בִּרְכְתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">רְ</span>אוּבֵן דְּלָא יְמוּת וִיקַבְּלוּן בְּנוֹהִי אַחְסַנְתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">ה</span>וֹדָא לִיהוּדָה לְמֶעֱבַד לְסָנְאוֹהִי פּוּרְעָנוּתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">מְ</span>הֵימָן אִשְׁתְּכַח לֵוִי דְּנַסִּיתָהִי עַל מֵי מַצּוּתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">מַ</span>גֵּין עַל בִּנְיָמִין וּבְאַרְעֵיהּ תִּשְׁרֵי שְׁכִינְתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">אֲ</span>מָר לְיוֹסֵף דִּמְנַשֶּׁה אַלְפַיָּא וּדְאֶפְרַיִם רִבְּוָתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">יִ</span>קְרַיָּא דִּזְבוּלוּן וּדְיִשָּׂשכָר לָייְפֵי בְּטוּרָא דְבֵיתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">רֵ</span>ישׁ עַמָּא עָאל גָד וְאִתְקַבַּל דִּילֵיהּ בְּקַדְמֵיתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">וּ</span>לְדָן אֲמַר תַּקִּיף דָּן כְּגוּר אַרְיָוָתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">יָ</span>ם גִּנֵּיסַר מַעֲרָבוֹהִי וְדָרוֹמוֹהִי לְנַפְתָּלִי יְרוּתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">עַ</span>ל־כׇּל־בְּנַיָּא בְּרִיךְ אָשֵׁר תׇּקְפָּא כְּעוּלֵימָתָּא\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nThe prophet of prophets said on the day he received death <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nBlessings for all the tribes, for each son of the whole<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_20');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_20');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_20\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[20]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_20\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Jacob&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_20').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_20', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> he gave one blessing:<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_21');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_21');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_21\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[21]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_21\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> All of the following twelve lines, up to &#8220;the dew of good,&#8221; are based on Onkelos&#8217; translation of the blessings in Deuteronomy 33.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_21').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_21', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nReuben should not die, and his sons should receive an inheritance. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nSplendor to Judah, to do retribution on those who hate him. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nLevi was found faithful, as he was tested at the waters of strife. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nA shield on Benjamin, in whose land <span class=\"divine-referent\">the Presence</span> dwells. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nHe said to Joseph that Manasseh had thousands, Ephraim myriads. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nHonors of Zebulun, with Issachar joined, on the mountain of the House. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nFirst of the people Gad entered, receiving what was his first. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nTo Dan he said: Dan is mighty as a lion&#8217;s whelp. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nThe Galilee&#8217;s west and south are Naphtali&#8217;s portion. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nOver all sons blessed is Asher, strong as youth. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span class=\"acrostic\">לֵ</span>ית אֱלָהּ כֶּאֱלָהָנָא בִּשְׁמַיָּא לֵיהּ שְׁכִינְתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">חֲ</span>מָר וְעִבוּר אַרְעָא עָבְדָא בְּטַלָּא דְּטַבְתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">זְ</span>גֵי מֹשֶׁה בָּתַר דְּנָא וַאֲתָא שָׂרָא דְּמוֹתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">קַ</span>בֵּיל נַפְשֵׁיהּ בִּצְרָרָא דְּחַיֵּי בְּפַרְדֵּיס גִּנְתָּא\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nThere is no god but <span class=\"divine-referent\">our God</span>, whose <span class=\"divine-referent\">Presence</span> is in heaven. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nWine and grain the land makes with the dew of good. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nMoshe lay down after this and the prince of death came. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nHe received his soul in the bond of life in the paradise garden. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span class=\"acrostic\">וְ</span>כֵן בִּרְשׁוּת חַכִּימֵי עַם בְּיוֹם חֶדְוָתָא דְּאוֹרָיְתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">אֲ</span>תַרְגֵּם בְּיוֹמָא דֵּין תְּרֵי סִדְרֵי דַּחֲתִימוּתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">מִ</span>בַּתְרָאָה עַד־רֵישָׁא וּמֵאִיבְלָא עַד־קַדְמִיתָּא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">נְ</span>בִיָּא רַבָּא אַיְקַר בְּתַרְגוּם וְדָא בִרְכְּתָּא\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nAnd thus, with permission of the sages of the people, on the day of the rejoicing of the Torah, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nI will translate today two orders of sealing, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nFrom the last to the first, and from mourning to beginning. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nThe great prophet I will honor with the translation of &#8220;And this is the blessing&#8230;&#8221; <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div class=\"speaker-mute footnotes_reference_container\"> <div class=\"footnote_container_prepare\"><p><span role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_reference_container_label pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_expand_collapse_reference_container__1();\">Notes</span><span role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_reference_container_collapse_button\" style=\"display: none;; display: none;\" onclick=\"footnote_expand_collapse_reference_container__1();\"></span></p></div> <div id=\"footnote_references_container__1\" style=\"\"><table class=\"footnotes_table footnote-reference-container\"><caption class=\"accessibility\">Notes</caption> <tbody> \r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_1\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_1');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >1</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Shmini Atseret is distinguished from Sukkot in six ways.</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_2\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_2');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >2</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Sukkah 48a</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_3\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_3');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >3</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Shavuot, also called “Gathering” in rabbinic texts.</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_4\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_4');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >4</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Shir haShirim Rabbah 2:11:1</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_5\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_5');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >5</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Sukkah 55b</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_6\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_6');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >6</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">I Kings 8:65</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_7\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_7');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >7</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">I Kings 8:64</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_8\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_8');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >8</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Solomon</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_9\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_9');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >9</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">I Kings 8:65</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_10\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_10');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >10</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Ezra</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_11\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_11');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >11</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Nehemiah</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_12\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_12');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >12</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Nehemiah 8:18</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_13\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_13');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >13</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">An expression of self-reproach. Find Jeremiah 31:19</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_14\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_14');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >14</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Rosh haShanah</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_15\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_15');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >15</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Yom Kippur</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_16\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_16');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >16</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Deuteronomy, which is largely the final speech of Moses. Find Deuteronomy 17:18.</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_17\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_17');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >17</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Kiddushin 38a</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_18\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_18');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >18</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Adar</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_19\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_19');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >19</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Targum Pseudo-Jonathan on Deuteronomy 34:6</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_20\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_20');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >20</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Jacob</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_21\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_21');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >21</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">All of the following twelve lines, up to &#8220;the dew of good,&#8221; are based on Onkelos&#8217; translation of the blessings in Deuteronomy 33.</td></tr>\r\n\r\n </tbody> </table> </div></div><script type=\"text/javascript\"> function footnote_expand_reference_container__1() { jQuery('#footnote_references_container__1').show(); jQuery('#footnote_reference_container_collapse_button__1').text('−'); } function footnote_collapse_reference_container__1() { jQuery('#footnote_references_container__1').hide(); jQuery('#footnote_reference_container_collapse_button__1').text('+'); } function footnote_expand_collapse_reference_container__1() { if (jQuery('#footnote_references_container__1').is(':hidden')) { footnote_expand_reference_container__1(); } else { footnote_collapse_reference_container__1(); } } function footnote_moveToReference__1(p_str_TargetID) { footnote_expand_reference_container__1(); var l_obj_Target = jQuery('#' + p_str_TargetID); if (l_obj_Target.length) { jQuery( 'html, body' ).delay( 0 ); jQuery('html, body').animate({ scrollTop: l_obj_Target.offset().top - window.innerHeight * 0.2 }, 380); } } function footnote_moveToAnchor__1(p_str_TargetID) { footnote_expand_reference_container__1(); var l_obj_Target = jQuery('#' + p_str_TargetID); if (l_obj_Target.length) { jQuery( 'html, body' ).delay( 0 ); jQuery('html, body').animate({ scrollTop: l_obj_Target.offset().top - window.innerHeight * 0.2 }, 380); } }</script>",
